(a)(4) — a family or trust transferee, or a death-or-divorce circumstance
=========================================================================

6 ways this can be satisfied.

  1. transfer's to a member of the family of the purchaser or the equivalent
  2. transfer's to a trust controlled by the purchaser
  3. transfer's to a trust created for the benefit of a member of the family of the purchaser or the equivalent
  4. transfer's in connection with death of the purchaser
  5. transfer's in connection with divorce of the purchaser
  6. transfer's in connection with a circumstance similar to death or divorce of the purchaser
